<!--
  Endless-spool status line: will a runout switch to a backup spool, and if not,
  why not.

  Entirely subject-driven — AmsState::sync_endless_spool_from_backend() writes
  ams_endless_state (helix::printer::EndlessSpoolStatusKind) and ams_endless_text
  (the translated sentence), so this component needs no C++ of its own and can be
  dropped into any panel or menu that has room for one line.

  State 0 (Hidden) is the "this printer has no such mechanism" case, and is the
  only state with nothing truthful to say — hence a flag binding rather than a
  structural <if>: the subtree is one icon and one label, so building it and
  hiding it is cheaper than rebuilding it on every backend swap.

  hide_when_healthy (0/1): the AMS panel passes 1 so the healthy sentence is
  not permanently on screen — there the line surfaces only for attention kinds
  (Off, Unknown, NeedsPlugin). The context menu leaves it off: its job is
  explaining the greyed backup dropdown, including when it is greyed because
  everything already works. The value is spliced into the cond expression as
  an int literal, so it must stay numeric.

  The text may carry an embedded newline (the restriction reason on its own
  line), which is why the label is long_mode="wrap" and the row is height="content".
  That is also what keeps the long German/French/Portuguese/Russian restriction
  strings from clipping at 480x272 — they gain a second line instead of a
  truncated first one.

  One binding owns the hidden flag for both conditions: flag bindings set AND
  clear on every subject change, so a second bind_flag_if_eq for the On case
  would fight this one and the last-registered would win in every state.
-->
<component>
  <api>
    <prop name="hide_when_healthy" type="int" default="0"/>
  </api>
  <view extends="lv_obj"
        width="100%" height="content" style_pad_all="0" style_pad_gap="#space_xs" scrollable="false" clickable="false"
        flex_flow="row" style_flex_main_place="start" style_flex_cross_place="start">
    <bind_flag_if flag="hidden" cond="ams_endless_state eq 0 or (${hide_when_healthy} and ams_endless_state eq 1)"/>
    <icon src="infinity" size="xs" variant="secondary"/>
    <text_small name="endless_status_text"
                bind_text="ams_endless_text" flex_grow="1" long_mode="wrap" style_text_color="#text_muted"/>
  </view>
</component>
